## 4. Factual, Statutory & Regulatory Citations
* **Mandatory BIS Hallmarking & HUID:** Cites the Government of India April 1, 2023 mandate requiring the 3-part hallmark on all gold jewellery: (1) Triangular BIS logo, (2) Purity mark (`22K916` or `18K750`), and (3) 6-character laser-engraved alphanumeric Hallmark Unique Identification (HUID), verifiable via the official BIS CARE mobile app.
* **Legal Metrology (Packaged Commodities) Rules:** Details statutory net gold weight billing protections. Explicitly explains that stones, pearls, lac resin wax filler, and zari threads must never be weighed or billed at precious gold rates.
* **Taxation & Pricing Breakdown:** Accurately details the 4-component jewellery pricing formula: `[Net Gold Weight × Live Board Rate] + [Gemstone Cost] + [Making Charges] + [3% Unified GST]`.

